WEBVTT

00:58.099 --> 01:00.060
Signals are simple.

01:01.811 --> 01:04.189
Sometimes, they're sounds.

01:05.065 --> 01:07.233
Sometimes, they're colors.

01:34.010 --> 01:34.844
HA-KYUNG

01:34.928 --> 01:37.931
And sometimes, they're vibrations.

01:38.014 --> 01:44.062
They keep signaling to me
that nothing is safe in this world.

01:45.814 --> 01:52.821
EPISODE 1
SIGNAL

01:56.491 --> 01:58.118
- No answer?
- Mm.

02:00.662 --> 02:03.123
Sorry. I don't think
I can make it to the hanbok store.

02:03.206 --> 02:05.333
- I'm not feeling good.
- What is it?

02:06.376 --> 02:08.211
Ki-jun doesn't feel so great today.

02:08.795 --> 02:09.796
Or he's upset.

02:11.172 --> 02:12.257
"Upset"?

02:13.424 --> 02:15.051
About yesterday.

02:15.677 --> 02:17.303
Why did she drag him around for that long?

02:17.387 --> 02:19.889
Not only drag him around.

02:19.973 --> 02:23.434
All day long, she kept
messing around with his ego.

02:23.518 --> 02:26.354
Mm, if I was him, I'd be
so appalled, I'd call the wedding off.

02:26.437 --> 02:28.731
Oh, I'd be grateful for that.

02:28.815 --> 02:30.733
Mom.

02:30.817 --> 02:33.528
It's hard these days
to find a decent man, you know.

02:33.611 --> 02:36.573
A steady paycheck,
pension guaranteed at retirement,

02:36.656 --> 02:39.284
guaranteed you'll never starve.

02:40.160 --> 02:42.954
That's why
she's marrying him. It's his stability.

02:43.037 --> 02:45.540
At least be a little reliable
for her, you know.

02:45.623 --> 02:48.543
I barely dragged him around all yesterday,
and now he's not feeling great?

02:48.626 --> 02:50.795
I feel fantastic and I'm almost 70.

02:51.379 --> 02:52.964
"Stability" my ass!

02:53.047 --> 02:55.550
Just think of it
as fate for them.

02:55.633 --> 02:58.761
Mom, look, they've been together
ten whole years without one fight.

02:58.845 --> 03:00.889
Yeah. And that's also not good.

03:00.972 --> 03:04.184
I'm her mother,
and even I can't stand her attitude.

03:04.267 --> 03:05.852
Even if he's so in love,

03:05.935 --> 03:08.146
it's a little suspicious
he never gets irritated.

03:08.229 --> 03:10.815
It's true love. It's true!

03:10.899 --> 03:13.443
Couples argue to show
they love each other.

03:14.694 --> 03:16.112
This one, I like it.

03:16.196 --> 03:18.573
- Yeah, it's pretty.
- The color is really beautiful.

03:18.656 --> 03:20.909
Excuse me.

03:21.618 --> 03:23.244
- Ah, yes, ma'am.
- Ah!

03:23.328 --> 03:24.746
- Right this way.
- Thanks.

03:28.374 --> 03:31.753
Daytime temperatures today
are up over three degrees nationwide.

03:31.836 --> 03:33.379
Expect more of sunny skies.

03:33.463 --> 03:35.548
We've got scattered clouds
across the region right now.

03:35.632 --> 03:36.799
But they're almost cleared up,

03:36.883 --> 03:40.470
and then it stayed clear and bright
for a good while after that.

03:40.553 --> 03:43.514
Air quality is high,
so enjoy that spring sunshine.

03:43.598 --> 03:45.808
- Lovely weather in Seoul with a height…
- Are we there yet?

03:45.892 --> 03:46.976
- …of 18 degrees.
- Huh?

03:47.060 --> 03:49.062
But it's a light midday breeze,
too, for a little afternoon…

03:49.145 --> 03:51.105
- Oh, up there, turn left.
- We will have the weather

03:51.189 --> 03:52.941
you wish you could have every day.

03:53.024 --> 03:57.195
As the sunshine continues,
brush conditions will get drier.

03:57.278 --> 03:58.696
So, everyone, watch those embers…

04:06.746 --> 04:08.248
You said we were going for tea.

04:08.998 --> 04:10.166
We are here for tea.

04:11.709 --> 04:14.587
- Is this a teahouse, Mom?
- What makes something a teahouse?

04:14.671 --> 04:17.006
If we're inside and drinking tea,
that makes it a teahouse.

04:23.179 --> 04:26.224
What are you seeking?
What has brought you here today?

04:26.307 --> 04:28.935
Uh, my daughter, I mentioned her earlier.

04:29.018 --> 04:31.729
- Oh, this is her.
- You know, she's a deaconess.

04:32.313 --> 04:33.564
"Deaconess?"

04:33.648 --> 04:37.277
Deaconess, pastor, doctor,
reverend, professor.

04:37.360 --> 04:40.571
All titles people seek
when they have a conflicted heart.

04:42.115 --> 04:44.742
Oh, here.

04:47.078 --> 04:50.456
Mm. Both born under the Red Hare.

04:53.042 --> 04:54.836
Year and hour of the hare.

05:02.552 --> 05:06.556
Being too cautious
can cause some problems in your life.

05:07.682 --> 05:10.768
She's so skeptical
ever since she was little.

05:10.852 --> 05:13.980
She'd even smell the cup
before she'd have a drink of water.

05:14.063 --> 05:16.691
I just don't want to turn out
like Papa. What's wrong with that?

05:16.774 --> 05:17.859
Hey now.

05:17.942 --> 05:19.777
Mom's just worried about you.

05:19.861 --> 05:22.905
And you should know your true
astral compatibility before you marry.

05:22.989 --> 05:25.033
So you got divorced
'cause the stars weren't aligned?

05:25.116 --> 05:27.618
Ha-kyung, don't say that.

05:27.702 --> 05:28.703
So your daughter.

05:29.912 --> 05:31.497
You're obviously a little cautious.

05:31.581 --> 05:33.916
A little cautious.
Yes, you're right. She is.

05:34.000 --> 05:37.295
More than a little.
It's almost an affliction.

05:37.378 --> 05:42.383
But an astral connection can't be avoided
just because you're cautious.

05:50.600 --> 05:51.434
What? What now?

05:51.517 --> 05:54.312
- The husband's journey…
- What about it?

05:55.813 --> 05:58.024
His relationship with his spouse
isn't great.

05:58.107 --> 05:59.984
Also, I can see
yang-in energy in him.

06:00.068 --> 06:02.820
His wife, he could lose her.

06:03.404 --> 06:04.947
- A dead wife?
- Divorce?

06:07.909 --> 06:09.619
Ah, I was right.

06:09.702 --> 06:12.163
I told you something was wrong
about him from the beginning.

06:12.246 --> 06:13.831
- I'm done here.
- Hey, Ha-kyung.

06:13.915 --> 06:15.249
- Stay and hear her out.
- Let go!

06:15.333 --> 06:16.376
- Hey!
- I paid a lot of money for this.

06:16.459 --> 06:19.003
Bring that umbrella over there.

06:19.712 --> 06:21.672
Why?

06:23.091 --> 06:24.467
It's going to rain.

06:46.406 --> 06:47.698
Rain? I don't think so.

06:56.040 --> 06:57.500
SI-WOO

06:57.583 --> 06:59.669
Si means time and woo means rain.

06:59.752 --> 07:01.712
It means rain that comes on time.

07:01.796 --> 07:05.299
Hmm. So that's why woo is used for rain.

07:05.383 --> 07:08.636
Ah, you know, as a name,
it's not really done.

07:08.719 --> 07:12.265
Oh! My grandfather
was a farmer his whole life.

07:12.348 --> 07:15.810
He said that nothing's more precious
than rain that comes just in time.

07:16.853 --> 07:19.439
And, uh, why do you need a seal?

07:23.401 --> 07:24.485
I'm buying a new car.

07:27.196 --> 07:28.865
STAMP SEALS

08:01.856 --> 08:03.107
Doors opening.

08:06.444 --> 08:08.446
Doors closing.

08:17.580 --> 08:18.831
PASSCODE ERROR

08:32.220 --> 08:34.639
Oh! What are you doing here right now?

08:34.722 --> 08:36.807
You said you weren't feeling good. Here.

08:36.891 --> 08:39.227
I'm feeling better after a cold shower.

08:39.310 --> 08:40.394
Uh-huh. That's good to hear.

08:41.771 --> 08:43.564
How come you changed the door code?

08:45.024 --> 08:46.901
Oh, uh, that's…

08:47.568 --> 08:49.195
My mom barged in on you, huh?

08:51.239 --> 08:53.407
Sorry.

08:53.491 --> 08:56.369
- Ah, you comin' in?
- I gotta get to work.

08:56.452 --> 08:58.079
I'm already running late.

08:58.162 --> 08:59.288
Just a sec.

09:01.791 --> 09:02.833
I've got to run.

09:02.917 --> 09:04.544
- Make sure you eat the porridge.
- Mm.

09:06.295 --> 09:07.630
Doors opening.

09:08.714 --> 09:10.591
Hello. Jin Ha-kyung speaking.

09:11.425 --> 09:12.677
Doors closing.

09:19.517 --> 09:21.602
You should report to the Director.

09:21.686 --> 09:23.688
I thought we said
we wouldn't talk about that.

09:23.771 --> 09:25.773
Come on, though. For real. It's hail.

09:26.315 --> 09:28.901
The serious hail,
there'd be guaranteed city damage.

09:28.985 --> 09:32.029
So we need to run analysis
and even if it's just one percent chance.

09:32.113 --> 09:35.032
So, Asst. Director, what's the probability
from your initial tracking?

09:36.033 --> 09:37.994
- You wanna hear a number?
- Yes.

09:39.245 --> 09:41.163
Around nearly five percent.

09:41.247 --> 09:43.207
Okay. And without a round nearly?

09:47.003 --> 09:48.087
HAIL RADAR

09:49.922 --> 09:52.174
Somewhere between 4.8 and 4.9.

09:52.258 --> 09:54.427
So you're telling me
it's still under five percent.

09:54.510 --> 09:56.429
I'm saying it's super close, though.

09:56.512 --> 09:58.097
Well, circle back
when it's really five, okay?

09:58.180 --> 10:00.391
We really should do this by the book.
You understand?

10:05.813 --> 10:07.481
She acts like she's the director.

10:15.698 --> 10:17.575
DIRECTOR CHOI JONG-SU

10:52.485 --> 10:54.654
On your way to work, Reporter Chae?

10:59.325 --> 11:01.410
- What's with the car?
- I bought it.

11:02.203 --> 11:04.538
- With what money?
- I got a three-year loan.

11:06.582 --> 11:08.501
Come on. Get in, huh?

11:08.584 --> 11:10.002
I gotta go.

11:14.423 --> 11:16.592
They already wrapped up
the morning forecast

11:16.676 --> 11:17.885
and it's almost lunchtime.

11:18.678 --> 11:20.513
You gotta eat something, right, hmm?

11:22.473 --> 11:23.766
So let's go.

11:40.116 --> 11:41.492
It's not new?

11:42.535 --> 11:44.245
It's essentially new.

11:44.328 --> 11:45.830
Just a little not new.

12:06.684 --> 12:09.145
You saw this place on TV and you said
you wanted to come here.

12:09.770 --> 12:10.896
What do you think?

12:10.980 --> 12:12.773
Your boyfriend's so observant, huh?

12:12.857 --> 12:14.483
Oh.

12:17.153 --> 12:18.320
Oh, you're back.

12:18.404 --> 12:19.864
Uh…

12:22.950 --> 12:26.245
- We'll have the number two Couple Special.
- Great. Couple number two.

12:26.328 --> 12:27.955
Mm-hmm.

12:29.915 --> 12:33.127
- You've been here before?
- Uh, with a friend.

12:34.336 --> 12:35.963
Ah. Oh, well.

12:36.046 --> 12:38.257
I wanted to bring you for your first time.

12:38.340 --> 12:39.425
Mm.

12:39.508 --> 12:40.843
That was so long ago.

12:40.926 --> 12:43.471
Now that I've got a car,
I'll start taking you out more.

12:44.138 --> 12:45.431
What would you like to go do?

12:46.557 --> 12:48.225
Mm, I don't know.

12:48.309 --> 12:50.311
Mm…

12:51.145 --> 12:52.354
Ah! Road trip?

12:53.647 --> 12:57.067
It's summer soon.
Let's go before it gets too crazy.

12:58.986 --> 13:00.529
A few days ago,

13:00.613 --> 13:03.365
there was a faint signal
on the adiabatic report.

13:03.449 --> 13:04.366
You know that one?

13:05.618 --> 13:07.161
In the middle of March, a snow warning?

13:07.244 --> 13:09.079
Right away, I knew that it had to be hail.

13:09.163 --> 13:11.290
I knew I had to find the data
to back up my report,

13:11.373 --> 13:13.542
so I spent most
of three whole days in the…

13:19.256 --> 13:20.257
Ah.

13:22.009 --> 13:23.302
You like Gapyeong, right?

13:23.385 --> 13:24.970
There are so many
cute cafés there.

13:25.054 --> 13:28.307
We could bring a tent and cookware
and camp outside somewhere with a view.

13:28.390 --> 13:31.435
I know everything there is about
the geography and weather over there.

13:31.519 --> 13:33.562
Uh, camping's not for me.

13:35.356 --> 13:37.316
Or a vacation rental?
Bet there's a good one.

13:42.571 --> 13:43.656
Okay, uh…

13:49.954 --> 13:51.121
Damn.

13:51.205 --> 13:53.457
Hail. No way.

13:54.291 --> 13:55.292
Oh.

13:55.376 --> 13:57.127
The forecast was clear.

13:59.296 --> 14:00.464
They ignored us again.

14:39.128 --> 14:43.173
PREVENT FOREST FIRES

14:46.886 --> 14:48.137
Situation Room, do you copy?

14:48.220 --> 14:51.891
The hail is damaging the helo airframe.
Repeat. Helicopter airframe damaged.

15:06.322 --> 15:09.491
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

15:09.575 --> 15:12.036
TREAT THE SKIES AS A FRIEND
AND THE PEOPLE AS THE SKIES

15:13.996 --> 15:15.205
Yes. I understand.

15:15.873 --> 15:17.458
Yes, sir. Yes.

15:18.667 --> 15:21.045
Yes, we will report back. Yes.

15:23.923 --> 15:25.007
Ah, goodness.

15:26.467 --> 15:29.011
Not a single person
alerted me this morning.

15:29.595 --> 15:30.471
Sorry, sir.

15:30.554 --> 15:32.973
Until late this morning,
the atmosphere was stable

15:33.057 --> 15:35.476
and vertical temperature change
was expected to be very light.

15:36.060 --> 15:38.896
But surface temperatures rose
and stability became very poor.

15:38.979 --> 15:41.857
How did you analyze the AWS,
state and vertical wind field?

15:41.941 --> 15:44.193
- There weren't any hail signals…
- Do you feel bad yet?

15:44.276 --> 15:45.694
…from the analysis results.

15:49.198 --> 15:50.783
But if we analyze the data

15:50.866 --> 15:53.619
from three hours ago,
or at least three perhaps…

15:54.662 --> 15:57.039
Hey. Aren't you off today?

15:57.706 --> 15:58.874
Your money, please.

15:59.375 --> 16:00.960
I'm in the middle of a meeting.

16:01.543 --> 16:04.588
I told you. I told you
it was hail on the report.

16:04.672 --> 16:08.550
With hail this bad, there must
have been an indicator signal somewhere.

16:09.259 --> 16:10.344
How frustrating.

16:11.095 --> 16:13.847
Let me see the adiabatic charts
in the affected area.

16:13.931 --> 16:15.808
Starting six hours ago.

16:15.891 --> 16:17.559
Mm-hmm.

16:17.643 --> 16:18.727
Um…

16:20.562 --> 16:21.939
Uh, okay, then. Twelve hours.

16:22.022 --> 16:23.315
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

16:24.692 --> 16:26.235
Now bring up three hours ago.

16:26.777 --> 16:29.363
Mm. Suwon.

16:30.030 --> 16:31.657
Not there. Incheon.

16:36.787 --> 16:37.830
Icheon.

16:39.206 --> 16:40.416
Hey, wait a minute. That one.

16:40.499 --> 16:42.960
On the bottom. Zoom in a little.

16:54.722 --> 16:55.848
Isn't that it?

16:57.099 --> 16:59.893
Uh-huh, signal's right there.

16:59.977 --> 17:01.186
See?

17:01.729 --> 17:04.189
My goodness.

17:06.066 --> 17:08.110
Yeah. You could see the clouds moving.

17:10.279 --> 17:12.322
Ah! Ah…

17:12.406 --> 17:13.699
Huh? Hmm?

17:16.702 --> 17:18.787
You said it was real
as a ghost eating rice

17:18.871 --> 17:21.999
when I came over to show it to you.
Can you see it now? Obvious hail.

17:22.541 --> 17:24.168
All right. I'll buy you coffee.

17:24.251 --> 17:26.670
Huh? Just coffee?

17:27.921 --> 17:30.924
Director doesn't mean rich, you know.

17:31.008 --> 17:33.802
- Here, take it.
- Ah, no, no.

17:33.886 --> 17:35.054
Coffee's fine.

17:35.679 --> 17:37.848
- Thank you.
- Sure.

17:41.143 --> 17:43.854
- That's all. Well, then, bye. Go.
- O… okay.

17:43.937 --> 17:45.606
- Uh-huh. Yeah.
- Wait, um…

17:47.066 --> 17:48.984
Director Choi, had you seen this?

17:55.657 --> 17:56.575
I had.

17:57.743 --> 18:01.246
But I thought it was
just a temporary phenomenon.

18:01.330 --> 18:04.416
You can make your own judgment calls.

18:04.500 --> 18:07.127
But it should have at least
been mentioned in this report.

18:07.211 --> 18:09.588
- Sir, the numbers indicate--
- I'm sorry, sir.

18:09.671 --> 18:12.382
It was my fault. I'll start a report now.

18:14.927 --> 18:18.388
Call the Aviation Meteorologist
and say it was our mistake.

18:19.306 --> 18:21.850
Reach out to the Expressway Corporation
and the RDA,

18:21.934 --> 18:23.936
and find out about any crop damage.

18:24.019 --> 18:25.646
Yes, sir.

18:26.855 --> 18:28.232
A short phenomenon?

18:28.315 --> 18:31.819
You think saying nonsense will cover up
you missing all the signs?

18:35.322 --> 18:36.740
We don't just broadcast the weather.

18:36.824 --> 18:38.909
We're meant to forecast it,
for God's sake.

18:41.078 --> 18:42.621
I can't believe this.

18:45.541 --> 18:47.918
Sir, the reporters are waiting for us.

18:52.131 --> 18:54.007
Wonderful. I love that they're punctual.

18:56.385 --> 18:58.220
Director Choi, go handle it.

18:59.012 --> 19:00.931
I have to meet
the Administration Director.

19:36.925 --> 19:39.469
Sir, you know
that I told you about the hail.

19:39.553 --> 19:41.805
Could you put that in your report for me?

19:42.347 --> 19:43.807
What for?

19:43.891 --> 19:46.518
You said so yourself. The best
of the best are there, am I right?

19:47.895 --> 19:50.272
I wanna go.

19:50.355 --> 19:51.732
The best?

19:51.815 --> 19:53.734
Maybe years ago, man.

19:53.817 --> 19:54.985
What?

19:55.068 --> 19:59.364
It's changed a bit. I call it
Aoji Coal Mine that does weather.

20:04.244 --> 20:05.537
I was told you need these

20:05.621 --> 20:07.539
for the ex-post analysis of the hail.

20:07.623 --> 20:11.168
Uh, it's all the similar cases
since the 1990s.

20:11.919 --> 20:15.923
Uh, you know, our team's been here
overnight every day this week.

20:16.006 --> 20:19.009
Can't the Policy Office cover it?
Can you help us out?

20:19.092 --> 20:22.471
We would love to help you,
but, uh, Mr. Ko specifically said

20:22.554 --> 20:25.015
that he wants the report
to be from your team, though.

20:25.098 --> 20:27.392
So we have to analyze all that
and write a report

20:27.476 --> 20:28.977
and monitor the weather?

20:29.561 --> 20:31.438
- It's…
- When do you need it by?

20:31.521 --> 20:33.273
He wants it by this weekend.

20:33.357 --> 20:35.609
Thanks. Thanks a lot.

20:35.692 --> 20:37.319
Yeah. Run away, Park.

20:37.402 --> 20:39.571
Did you finish
the numerical model I asked for?

20:40.697 --> 20:43.283
- It'll be done soon.
- Finish it quickly.

20:50.374 --> 20:52.918
Maybe you should do
the briefing today, you know, huh?

20:53.001 --> 20:54.836
If you have a heart.

20:54.920 --> 20:57.422
I'd be overstepping authority
since the Chief Director's here.

20:58.382 --> 21:01.093
We've been the public's punching bag
forever, he's used to it.

21:09.893 --> 21:11.979
- Director Choi!
- Director Choi!

21:12.062 --> 21:13.730
- Oh, my god! What's going on?
- Oh, no!

21:13.814 --> 21:16.108
- Director Choi!
- What is happening?

21:16.191 --> 21:17.317
- I don't know.
- Sir!

21:17.401 --> 21:19.486
- Somebody call an ambulance!
- What happened? Did anyone see?

21:19.569 --> 21:21.029
- Someone get help!
- Director Choi!

21:37.504 --> 21:39.089
He'll be okay, think so?

21:39.172 --> 21:41.383
- I'm sure he's gonna make it.
- One moment.

21:42.384 --> 21:45.345
The Spokesperson's Office
is losing it. They want a meeting.

21:46.138 --> 21:49.516
They have to understand our
director just got taken to the hospital.

21:49.599 --> 21:51.727
How many ambulances have we had this year?

21:51.810 --> 21:54.730
What do we do? Someone has
to cover him and do the briefing.

22:02.738 --> 22:03.905
I can do it.

22:30.390 --> 22:31.600
How is Director Choi?

22:31.683 --> 22:33.560
Uh, they had to take him to the hospital.

22:33.643 --> 22:34.853
So we haven't heard.

22:35.395 --> 22:37.272
Who was that?

22:37.356 --> 22:39.483
Oh, just a reporter.

22:39.566 --> 22:42.527
She was asking me to change
the order of the questions.

22:42.611 --> 22:44.696
Hmm. What should I say?

22:44.780 --> 22:47.657
Hmm. They already did the basic briefing
about the hail today,

22:47.741 --> 22:50.369
- so you'll just fill in the details.
- Okay.

22:50.452 --> 22:51.411
Good luck.

23:06.635 --> 23:08.804
We will take some questions now.

23:15.769 --> 23:20.315
RESTRICTED AREA

23:23.402 --> 23:25.278
I'm at the hospital. Yeah.

23:25.987 --> 23:28.615
No, it sounds like
he's gonna be all right.

23:28.698 --> 23:29.699
Oh, one second.

23:29.783 --> 23:31.618
- Director Choi?
- Taking him to his room.

23:31.701 --> 23:33.537
- His room?
- Yes.

23:34.246 --> 23:36.456
Oh, Mrs. Choi. Are you okay?

23:36.998 --> 23:38.959
You didn't have to come.
You're always busy.

23:39.042 --> 23:40.168
Of course, I had to.

23:40.252 --> 23:42.629
- I'm so relieved it's not that bad.
- "Relieved"?

23:44.423 --> 23:45.340
Oh…

23:46.299 --> 23:50.470
He's been asking for a formal transfer
to the country for years now.

23:50.554 --> 23:51.805
Yeah.

23:51.888 --> 23:53.432
The doctor warned him a while ago

23:53.515 --> 23:55.642
that he had to be careful
and has high blood pressure.

23:56.226 --> 23:57.936
But you kept pushing, you kept pushing,

23:58.019 --> 24:00.397
saying, "Next year, we'll do it,"
every year.

24:00.981 --> 24:02.649
You're the reason why he landed here.

24:02.732 --> 24:04.401
Over what, a little hail?

24:04.484 --> 24:08.530
- It wasn't… There was more going on--
- I mean, you guys are always wrong.

24:08.613 --> 24:11.575
Why did you have to make it
a big deal this time?

24:11.658 --> 24:14.286
Do you know what they all call you?

24:15.454 --> 24:17.539
- What?
- A human juicer.

24:17.622 --> 24:20.083
Because you squeeze
people till there's nothing left.

24:21.168 --> 24:24.838
I'm exhausted, just like
everyone that works for you.

24:25.672 --> 24:28.008
I'm really…
I'm really sorry, you know that.

24:28.091 --> 24:30.594
Yeah. Well, goodbye, sir.

24:30.677 --> 24:33.054
- Yes. It'll be okay. I'm sorry.
- Thank you for coming.

24:42.355 --> 24:43.482
Any news?

24:48.153 --> 24:51.114
Uh, Director Choi had a heart attack.

24:52.574 --> 24:54.493
He kept saying that his chest felt heavy.

24:54.576 --> 24:55.660
He did?

24:56.870 --> 24:58.288
Why didn't I know that?

24:59.581 --> 25:02.083
They said he's gonna be okay, right?

25:02.167 --> 25:04.961
They're gonna do some extensive testing,
then we'll know more.

25:05.045 --> 25:06.213
He'll be okay, though.

25:06.296 --> 25:08.048
I don't want anyone calling him

25:08.131 --> 25:10.759
or going to visit him because we
don't want to stress him out, right?

25:10.842 --> 25:13.678
And while he's gone,
we'll put an interim on Team Two.

25:16.097 --> 25:17.599
Jin, you can do it.

25:21.102 --> 25:22.938
Sir, I'm getting married next month.

25:23.980 --> 25:26.358
You can manage till Mr. Choi returns, huh?

25:26.858 --> 25:27.984
For two weeks tops.

25:28.068 --> 25:29.819
So can you handle all that?

25:31.571 --> 25:33.949
She can barely handle what she does now.

25:34.032 --> 25:35.992
Huh? Whoa. Speak up.

25:36.076 --> 25:38.453
If you have a better idea, say it. What?

25:39.454 --> 25:41.039
- No, sir.
- Okay.

25:42.290 --> 25:45.502
That's the plan, then, okay? Great.

25:51.466 --> 25:52.884
Okay, then.

26:23.206 --> 26:24.624
Hey, you on your way?

26:24.708 --> 26:27.752
No, I can't. I can't get away
for the reunion.

26:29.170 --> 26:30.922
Again? I can't go alone.

26:31.006 --> 26:34.342
I don't have a choice.
Director Choi is on a leave of absence.

26:43.393 --> 26:44.853
I get it.

26:44.936 --> 26:47.897
I'll tell them you say hi.
Just focus on your work.

26:49.274 --> 26:52.235
It sounds like it's just for two weeks,
so we just have to make it till then.

26:53.069 --> 26:54.154
Okay.

27:09.669 --> 27:16.676
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

28:00.178 --> 28:01.554
Wow.

28:01.638 --> 28:02.889
It's incredible.

28:08.395 --> 28:10.271
I wish Yu-jin can see this.

28:27.163 --> 28:28.415
GLOBAL WARMING
AND THE IMPACT OF CLIMATE CHANGE

28:28.498 --> 28:31.710
So basically,
it's gonna be hot this summer.

28:31.793 --> 28:32.877
It needs to be simpler.

28:32.961 --> 28:35.380
Like, "Worst summer ever."

28:35.463 --> 28:36.923
"Get ready to sweat."

28:37.006 --> 28:38.550
"Heat like a steam bath."

28:38.633 --> 28:41.386
Keep it to five syllables.
Your titles are too long.

28:41.469 --> 28:44.222
It's not that this summer's
gonna be especially hot.

28:44.305 --> 28:47.517
The average temperatures are rising.
One to two degrees from global warming.

28:47.600 --> 28:51.563
Oh, you really think people
give a crap about global warming?

28:51.646 --> 28:52.814
It just needs to be provocative.

28:52.897 --> 28:55.191
You need to think about
what average people read.

28:55.275 --> 28:57.736
- But then--
- Are you going to make me say it again?

28:57.819 --> 29:01.614
Okay. The goal is to make
air-conditioning sales go up.

29:01.698 --> 29:04.075
You know what company
has our biggest ad account?

29:04.159 --> 29:05.326
So we're an ad agency?

29:05.410 --> 29:07.120
Why don't we just report the weather?

29:07.203 --> 29:09.122
'Cause ads pay for you, they pay for me.

29:09.205 --> 29:10.749
How can we afford to be here?

29:10.832 --> 29:13.168
Keep that in mind, huh?

29:13.251 --> 29:15.336
And maybe we could get a bonus for once.

29:16.337 --> 29:17.505
Okay?

29:18.381 --> 29:19.674
Go on.

29:19.758 --> 29:21.634
You can do it, all right?

29:21.718 --> 29:22.719
Provocative.

29:35.273 --> 29:38.568
LEE SI-WOO

29:38.651 --> 29:40.779
- What?
- Look at these!

29:42.947 --> 29:44.365
I'M MAKING A SEAL TODAY
WHY?

29:44.449 --> 29:45.742
LOOK AT THESE VIEWS
THEY'RE NICE

29:50.038 --> 29:52.791
ISN'T IT AWESOME?

29:52.874 --> 29:54.918
Wow! I hit the jackpot today!

29:59.923 --> 30:01.382
That is a fairy cloud.

30:02.133 --> 30:05.345
I've only seen it once before.
I'm so lucky.

30:05.428 --> 30:06.805
Ugh.

30:09.390 --> 30:10.642
She saw them?

30:35.792 --> 30:37.502
Hey, Chief!

30:41.589 --> 30:44.843
Not this guy again.

30:44.926 --> 30:46.261
You win.

30:47.136 --> 30:48.137
I give up.

30:53.852 --> 30:57.272
So the antenna's operational
and nothing's wrong with it.

30:57.355 --> 30:59.399
But I could have told you that
on the phone.

30:59.482 --> 31:02.068
I had to see it
with my own eyes to trust it.

31:02.151 --> 31:04.863
And I really wanted to see you
in case you got lonely.

31:07.073 --> 31:09.284
So you think
that everything's operating well?

31:09.367 --> 31:10.785
Yes.

31:10.869 --> 31:13.413
You know the way out. I have work to do.

31:13.496 --> 31:15.748
It's just that we're only in March,

31:15.832 --> 31:19.460
and the temperatures are strangely low,
especially looking at inland averages.

31:19.544 --> 31:22.422
You have to go to the Gangwon Office.
They'll know.

31:26.384 --> 31:27.385
Oh.

31:27.468 --> 31:29.178
GANGWON REGIONAL OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

31:31.180 --> 31:32.265
Hello. How can I help you?

31:32.849 --> 31:35.894
Yes, hello. I saw surface temperatures
in Gangwon are off.

31:35.977 --> 31:37.103
Could you check them, please?

31:37.186 --> 31:38.646
Oh, yeah, sure.

31:39.647 --> 31:41.357
Yeah, and I also wanna know

31:41.441 --> 31:44.819
Pyeongchang, Chuncheon,
Hongcheon, Hoengseong, and Wonju.

31:44.903 --> 31:46.821
If you can.
If it's not too much trouble for you.

31:46.905 --> 31:49.782
Just a minute. Pyeongchang.

31:51.659 --> 31:52.744
Chuncheon.

31:53.661 --> 31:54.537
Hongcheon.

31:54.621 --> 31:55.872
And where else?

31:55.955 --> 31:57.290
Hoengseong and Wonju.

31:57.373 --> 31:59.918
Okay. Hoengseong and Wonju.

32:00.001 --> 32:02.337
- One moment.
- So sorry, but can you please hurry?

32:02.420 --> 32:04.714
- It's urgent.
- Wonju. Oh, no.

32:06.007 --> 32:07.675
Hello. This is Um.

32:08.259 --> 32:09.302
What is it?

32:09.385 --> 32:12.889
Yes, uh, I need Pyeongchang, Chuncheon,

32:12.972 --> 32:17.018
Hongcheon, Hoengseong,
and Wonju surface temperatures, please.

32:18.019 --> 32:19.312
GANGWON PROVINCE

32:19.395 --> 32:22.357
Oh, you're seeing wind coming in.

32:22.440 --> 32:24.275
It's a reaction to the sun's radiation.

32:24.359 --> 32:26.152
It happens from time to time.

32:26.235 --> 32:27.320
It'll level itself out.

32:27.403 --> 32:29.489
I don't think that's what's going on here.

32:29.572 --> 32:30.865
Huh?

32:32.492 --> 32:34.869
Well, thanks for your help.

32:35.703 --> 32:37.914
What do you mean by-- Are you there?

32:39.666 --> 32:41.793
What a rude little… Who was that?

32:41.876 --> 32:43.878
I, uh… I forgot to get his name.

32:45.171 --> 32:46.673
You forgot? That's important.

32:46.756 --> 32:49.884
If you knew his name, there's no way
some intern would talk to you that way.

32:50.635 --> 32:51.594
Sorry, sir.

32:51.678 --> 32:53.596
Jeez.

32:58.393 --> 33:00.311
- By the way, sir.
- Hmm?

33:00.395 --> 33:02.730
Did you hear the rumor coming from HQ?

33:02.814 --> 33:04.565
No. What happened?

33:04.649 --> 33:06.901
I heard that the director
for Team Two is out.

33:06.985 --> 33:08.319
They need a replacement.

33:10.029 --> 33:11.155
So what?

33:11.239 --> 33:13.658
You know, you have to go back someday.

33:14.450 --> 33:15.535
No, thanks.

33:16.119 --> 33:18.079
It was a pain in the ass.

33:18.162 --> 33:19.664
Even if they begged.

33:19.747 --> 33:22.875
Well, if you stay away from home too long,

33:22.959 --> 33:24.627
I heard your family
can forget who you are.

33:26.254 --> 33:28.006
Like you didn't exist.

33:46.524 --> 33:49.652
BO-MI'S DAD

33:58.453 --> 34:00.163
- Please. Oh.
- Hello?

34:00.663 --> 34:02.331
I didn't know if you were gonna answer me.

34:02.415 --> 34:04.042
What? You don't
always pick up when I call?

34:05.126 --> 34:06.419
Oh, well…

34:07.420 --> 34:08.463
Are things good?

34:09.047 --> 34:11.257
Well, could you do anything
if they weren't?

34:11.340 --> 34:13.176
Hey, don't do that.

34:13.259 --> 34:16.095
Be nice to your husband.
I haven't seen you in about--

34:16.179 --> 34:17.638
Why did you call?

34:18.514 --> 34:19.515
Bo-mi there?

34:20.641 --> 34:22.810
Bo-mi, it's Dad.

34:22.894 --> 34:23.936
No.

34:24.645 --> 34:27.231
- She can't.
- Oh, okay.

34:29.567 --> 34:30.568
'Kay. See you.

34:33.613 --> 34:36.115
- Sir!
- Mm?

34:36.199 --> 34:38.034
Something you should see.

34:38.117 --> 34:43.790
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

34:55.718 --> 34:57.845
- Not now. I'm busy.
- I'll be fast.

34:58.554 --> 35:00.598
Didn't you guys book Lian Wedding Hall?

35:00.681 --> 35:02.892
- Yeah, and why?
- Well, I called

35:02.975 --> 35:05.144
because Mom wanted me
to ask them something,

35:05.228 --> 35:07.563
and they never got your deposit.

35:07.647 --> 35:08.606
What?

35:08.689 --> 35:10.525
Ki-jun
won't even pick up the phone.

35:10.608 --> 35:12.151
Is everything okay with you?

35:12.235 --> 35:15.029
Ki-jun's so thorough.
It has to be a problem with the venue.

35:15.113 --> 35:17.490
- It's time, everyone.
- I'll look into it, okay? I gotta go.

35:20.535 --> 35:24.539
All right. What's, uh…

35:24.622 --> 35:26.207
What's that little dangler?

35:26.290 --> 35:29.252
Convective clouds formed
from an unstable atmosphere.

35:29.335 --> 35:31.045
And what's the humidity over there?

35:31.546 --> 35:33.965
It's, uh, around 82 percent, I believe.

35:34.465 --> 35:35.967
What's the chance it turns to rain?

35:36.050 --> 35:37.969
Well, below 30 percent, Director.

35:38.052 --> 35:40.680
Okay. That's below the threshold
to issue an alert.

35:41.264 --> 35:42.723
Okay. Let's do our meeting.

35:45.560 --> 35:47.520
We will now discuss March 14's report.

35:47.603 --> 35:49.689
Let's hear
from the Satellite Center first.

35:49.772 --> 35:53.317
Yes. Hello, Headquarters. If you look
at the current movement of the clouds,

35:53.401 --> 35:55.653
you could see that a band
is developing to the northeast.

35:55.736 --> 35:58.197
Gangwon Office, your opinion
on this, please.

35:58.823 --> 36:01.075
Well, judging
from the characteristics of the area,

36:01.159 --> 36:02.827
it is unlikely that it'll lead to rain.

36:03.578 --> 36:04.912
It's going to rain.

36:04.996 --> 36:06.330
I guarantee it!

36:06.414 --> 36:08.958
Damn.
So you're really going nuts again?

36:09.041 --> 36:11.169
Hey, can't you see the sky out there?

36:11.919 --> 36:13.337
I sent you all the data.

36:14.338 --> 36:16.382
A storm's brewing here.

36:16.465 --> 36:18.217
- Soon, it's gonna get worse.
- I see the smudge.

36:18.301 --> 36:20.887
Now go sit down.
We're talking about it on our call.

36:20.970 --> 36:23.681
- Just wait over there till we're done.
- We don't have time.

36:23.764 --> 36:26.225
We have to put out a heavy rain advisory
in the whole metro area right now.

36:26.309 --> 36:27.602
I said calm down.

36:27.685 --> 36:30.646
Look, right here, right here.
See how high the surface temperatures are?

36:30.730 --> 36:32.648
The Gangwon Office said
that it's temporary.

36:32.732 --> 36:34.025
But the instability is too strong,

36:34.108 --> 36:36.903
and there's a high chance that it turns
into a serious rainstorm.

36:36.986 --> 36:39.322
At this time, the…

36:39.405 --> 36:41.324
Look. Look here.

36:42.033 --> 36:43.367
But this…

36:48.581 --> 36:49.790
Metro Office, something to share?

36:49.874 --> 36:53.628
SEOUL METROPOLITAN OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

36:54.212 --> 36:58.257
The clouds that are forming
in the Gangwon area look unusual.

36:58.341 --> 37:00.509
Are you saying
that's a potential storm there?

37:00.593 --> 37:02.637
- Yes, in an hour.
- And your source?

37:04.805 --> 37:06.933
Uh, just a moment.

37:09.477 --> 37:11.479
An hour ago,
they were light clouds.

37:11.562 --> 37:14.982
However, passing the Chuncheon area,
they're rapidly approaching storm levels.

37:15.066 --> 37:16.692
I'll show you all the data right here.

37:28.955 --> 37:30.456
There he goes again.

37:32.583 --> 37:34.961
He's the one who predicted the hail.

37:35.670 --> 37:38.256
- And so?
- Consider that.

37:44.345 --> 37:47.056
Do you know how dry
the atmosphere is right now?

37:47.139 --> 37:49.684
Even if the rain clouds are large enough
to be caught as an echo,

37:49.767 --> 37:53.604
all of it will be evaporated
long before it arrives in the city.

37:53.688 --> 37:55.523
What if moisture
is added continuously

37:55.606 --> 37:57.566
as the formation continues
moving to the north?

38:00.653 --> 38:03.072
The temperature of the lower atmosphere
in this area is rising,

38:03.155 --> 38:05.533
so water vapor
is constantly being supplied.

38:05.616 --> 38:09.996
If you look at this, the clouds
were only two kilometers long an hour ago.

38:10.079 --> 38:13.082
But now, it's thicker.
Almost five or six kilometers.

38:13.165 --> 38:15.001
Furthermore, because
the surface temperature

38:15.084 --> 38:18.087
east of the metropolitan area is high
and the atmosphere is unstable,

38:18.170 --> 38:20.172
the clouds are more likely
to develop further

38:20.256 --> 38:22.300
as they move to this area
instead of evaporating.

38:22.383 --> 38:25.886
If all these numbers are correct,
then we have two to three hours

38:25.970 --> 38:28.639
before the entire metro area's storming.

38:33.769 --> 38:36.355
Then, according to you,
what's our chance of rain?

38:36.439 --> 38:38.316
Yes, so, uh…

38:38.399 --> 38:40.109
It should be about 18.7 or .8.

38:40.192 --> 38:42.945
- Yes, that's right.
- So you're saying…

38:43.029 --> 38:45.656
there's still well over
an 80 percent chance

38:45.740 --> 38:46.782
of clear skies today.

38:46.866 --> 38:50.453
The decimal, I would suggest,
isn't really necessary.

38:51.370 --> 38:55.124
Ah, well, then,
what's our course of action?

39:48.677 --> 39:50.012
I checked again

39:50.096 --> 39:52.515
and they're certain
that the deposit wasn't paid.

39:53.349 --> 39:55.935
They said that they told the groom
that the booking will be canceled

39:56.018 --> 39:58.145
if you don't pay the deposit
by end of the day.

40:03.818 --> 40:05.736
It's not even summertime.

40:05.820 --> 40:07.196
It's the middle of March.

40:07.279 --> 40:10.533
A storm alert of over 20 percent odds
is a pointless alarm.

40:10.616 --> 40:12.535
Even by your numbers, it's no concern.

40:13.452 --> 40:15.955
You keep talking about a seasonal formula.

40:16.038 --> 40:18.290
Don't you think the data's
more important than the month?

40:20.376 --> 40:22.503
Forecasting is about probability.

40:22.586 --> 40:24.630
- And that's why we're always wrong.
- What's that?

40:24.713 --> 40:26.090
From the 17th typhoon last summer

40:26.173 --> 40:29.051
to the fog of the beginning of this year,
and most recently, the hail.

40:29.135 --> 40:31.887
Look what happened because you
were too obsessed with probabilities.

40:31.971 --> 40:33.139
Why do we even have forecasters, then?

40:33.222 --> 40:35.808
Why not just read the averages
of the computers and post them?

40:39.437 --> 40:40.980
POWER OFF

40:42.356 --> 40:44.650
Weather is about flow.

40:44.733 --> 40:45.734
You can't throw that out

40:45.818 --> 40:47.445
'cause of a funny-looking signal,
you know.

40:48.320 --> 40:50.322
Sudden shifts
can always disrupt that flow.

40:50.406 --> 40:52.992
Even small changes
can ripple into huge sudden storms.

40:53.075 --> 40:54.452
Are you teaching us now?

40:55.286 --> 40:56.412
No.

40:56.495 --> 40:59.039
I'm just saying there's
a bigger problem here to address.

40:59.123 --> 41:01.625
Come on. That's it. Move.

41:02.543 --> 41:03.752
All right.

41:04.420 --> 41:06.046
Ha-kyung, substitute director.

41:06.797 --> 41:08.883
You should make a decision now.

41:16.599 --> 41:17.975
Let's do it like this.

41:24.523 --> 41:27.318
Metro Office has suggested
a reasonable hypothesis.

41:27.401 --> 41:29.737
However, 18's too low for a storm alert.

41:30.488 --> 41:33.657
There's not enough evidence
or precedent available.

41:33.741 --> 41:36.368
- I told you I would show you the data--
- That's it.

41:36.452 --> 41:38.370
Our office will make a final assessment

41:38.454 --> 41:40.623
on the metro alert
after watching for a little.

41:41.582 --> 41:45.252
During that time, the Metro Office
can provide us with their source data.

41:46.545 --> 41:48.506
Let's move on
to the weekend weather.

41:56.764 --> 41:58.140
Hey!

42:04.396 --> 42:07.066
He's not gonna let it go.

42:08.776 --> 42:10.861
- You know him?
- Lee Si-woo.

42:11.487 --> 42:14.198
I worked with him
on Baengnyeong Island when I started.

42:14.281 --> 42:17.034
- Hmm.
- He's usually a pretty mellow guy.

42:17.117 --> 42:20.829
But then, he has some unorthodox theory
and he won't shut up.

42:22.623 --> 42:23.916
But what bothers me is

42:24.500 --> 42:27.211
when he digs his heels in this hard,
sometimes he's right.

42:35.636 --> 42:37.763
Seok-ho, hey, it's me.

42:37.846 --> 42:39.181
What do you want?

42:39.265 --> 42:41.141
It's your job
to announce alerts, right?

42:42.393 --> 42:43.811
Yeah, it is. So what do you want?

42:44.770 --> 42:45.980
I just know a storm's here.

42:46.772 --> 42:48.274
Jeez, hey.

42:51.235 --> 42:52.987
I can't do it.

42:53.070 --> 42:56.073
You're really gonna let your office
ignore this like you did the hail?

42:56.156 --> 42:57.283
Hey, uh--

43:00.995 --> 43:02.955
I swear he's crazy.

43:04.999 --> 43:07.501
All right, then.
Uh, no other action items, right?

43:07.585 --> 43:08.544
No, sir.

43:08.627 --> 43:09.837
Mm-hmm. Okay.

43:09.920 --> 43:11.839
We'll adjourn the meeting here.

43:11.922 --> 43:13.716
- Thank you, sir.
- Thanks, everyone.

43:13.799 --> 43:15.301
- Thank you.
- Yes, thank you.

43:15.384 --> 43:16.969
Bye. See you tomorrow.

43:19.346 --> 43:22.016
Are you insane? What's your problem?

43:27.563 --> 43:28.480
What is it?

43:29.064 --> 43:32.192
The Metropolitan Office just put out
a storm advisory.

43:32.818 --> 43:33.819
What?

43:37.656 --> 43:38.616
You did this?

43:40.034 --> 43:43.621
Who would publish this without reporting
to the director first, huh?

43:43.704 --> 43:45.998
She won't accept my reports.
That's the reason why.

43:46.582 --> 43:48.250
Starting from the hail signal,

43:48.959 --> 43:50.628
she ignored me
and she said it was too low.

43:52.129 --> 43:53.547
What's he saying?

43:54.882 --> 43:58.135
There was a report from the Seoul
Metropolitan Office about a hail signal.

43:58.218 --> 44:01.555
The first one who detected it
was that guy you just spoke to.

44:02.723 --> 44:04.391
The probability was below five percent.

44:04.475 --> 44:06.143
It was five, if you rounded it out.

44:08.395 --> 44:11.273
Okay, so you declared
a strong weather alert

44:11.357 --> 44:14.360
without permission
from your director? Hmm?

44:14.443 --> 44:17.655
If you're gonna go rogue,
why do we pay for your superior?

44:17.738 --> 44:18.906
There's a hierarchy here.

44:18.989 --> 44:21.408
If you want to do things your way,
start your own company.

44:22.910 --> 44:24.286
I'm sorry, sir.

44:29.458 --> 44:32.670
An advisory has been issued.
So keep your posts.

44:33.962 --> 44:35.839
I need to talk with you.

44:35.923 --> 44:37.466
Yes, sir.

44:48.686 --> 44:50.104
My god.

44:57.194 --> 44:59.697
What do you mean
you didn't report to Director Choi?

45:01.073 --> 45:03.701
Like you heard, sir,
the probability was too low.

45:06.161 --> 45:07.371
What I meant…

45:08.205 --> 45:10.833
is why did you make that decision,
skipping the director?

45:10.916 --> 45:12.084
Why?

45:18.006 --> 45:19.091
Okay.

45:19.758 --> 45:21.343
Write a report on it.

45:23.345 --> 45:25.055
Shut your mouth.

45:25.139 --> 45:27.850
If it doesn't rain in an hour,
we're both completely dead.

45:27.933 --> 45:30.144
Don't worry. It's going to.

45:31.437 --> 45:32.354
Was it you?

45:33.689 --> 45:36.650
Are you the one who issued an advisory
without permission from Headquarters?

45:38.986 --> 45:40.821
Yes. It was me.

45:42.114 --> 45:45.325
Do you know how much it costs to declare
a single case of severe weather?

45:45.909 --> 45:48.162
And if it's wrong,
will you take the blame for it?

45:50.748 --> 45:52.166
And did you, the interim director,

45:52.249 --> 45:55.419
take full responsibility
for the incorrect hail forecast?

45:55.502 --> 45:56.712
What did you say?

45:56.795 --> 45:59.882
No, not incorrect. You didn't
report it to anyone at all, did you?

46:00.591 --> 46:02.426
I heard about
the whole situation.

46:02.509 --> 46:05.554
But, you know, even though you're busy
with all the wedding planning,

46:05.637 --> 46:08.599
isn't it a bit awkward
that a whole report was missed?

46:08.682 --> 46:11.935
You're a forecaster. You hold
the public's trust and confidence.

46:12.019 --> 46:14.730
You shouldn't throw that all away
because of your home life.

46:16.398 --> 46:18.650
- And you are?
- Lee Si-woo is my name.

46:19.568 --> 46:20.444
Lee Si-woo.

46:20.527 --> 46:23.322
You ask me to take responsibility
for this forecast?

46:23.405 --> 46:25.783
If I may share with you
my actual responsibilities,

46:25.866 --> 46:29.119
I predict and forecast weather
based on the data I have collected.

46:29.203 --> 46:31.246
I'm confident about my forecasts.

46:31.330 --> 46:34.666
Completely. And that confidence comes
from doing what I know is proper.

46:34.750 --> 46:36.668
That's true with the hail situation
as well.

46:36.752 --> 46:40.881
Oh, so you're saying you don't like
the way I've been doing my job here?

46:40.964 --> 46:42.966
Well, of course, you have
your wedding to think of,

46:43.050 --> 46:45.552
- so I do understand.
- Hey, you!

46:45.636 --> 46:47.262
It's Lee Si-woo, Metro Office.

46:49.515 --> 46:50.641
Hey, Lee Si-woo.

46:50.724 --> 46:52.559
Just don't leave there.

46:53.185 --> 46:55.020
Why? You coming here?

46:55.604 --> 46:56.897
Just don't.

46:56.980 --> 46:58.524
TRAFFIC MONITORING OFFICE

47:02.736 --> 47:04.488
Yes. Uh-huh.

47:10.077 --> 47:11.870
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:11.954 --> 47:14.540
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:15.999 --> 47:18.752
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:18.836 --> 47:21.004
EMERGENCY DUTY NOTIFICATION
MARCH 14

47:22.631 --> 47:24.716
ALL EMPLOYEES,
PLEASE REPORT TO EMERGENCY DUTIES

47:24.800 --> 47:26.009
UNTIL THE SITUATION IS RESOLVED

47:28.345 --> 47:30.848
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:33.308 --> 47:35.644
Heavy rain advisory
in all coastal areas.

47:36.311 --> 47:37.688
Patrol ships on duty.

47:37.771 --> 47:40.232
Provide nearby vessels of safety protocol.

47:40.315 --> 47:42.526
- Ship Two on the way.
- Loud and clear, understood.

47:52.995 --> 47:54.496
Double check that.

48:09.177 --> 48:11.221
They're inspecting our boats.
It's ridiculous.

48:11.305 --> 48:14.057
Okay. Inspect all you want.
We're not gonna go out. You're happy?

48:14.141 --> 48:15.642
Jeez.

48:17.728 --> 48:20.063
- Hey, over there.
- Get over here.

48:22.357 --> 48:24.026
Good.

48:30.365 --> 48:31.325
More water now?

48:40.834 --> 48:46.798
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY ISSUED
FOR METROPOLITAN AREA

48:46.882 --> 48:49.217
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

48:51.595 --> 48:53.430
SEOUL METROPOLITAN OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

48:57.434 --> 48:59.811
What now?

49:01.521 --> 49:05.692
Oh, that woman from Headquarters,
she won't actually come here, will she?

49:05.776 --> 49:07.527
There's no way she would, yeah.

49:09.321 --> 49:11.740
She was just angry at you
because you were being so…

49:11.823 --> 49:12.741
the way you always are.

49:13.742 --> 49:14.826
She's here.

49:23.043 --> 49:26.171
Uh, I'm gonna go smoke.
She's here to see you.

49:26.254 --> 49:27.881
- Bye.
- Mr. Lee Si-woo?

49:38.225 --> 49:40.727
- You're really here.
- Are we friends?

49:40.811 --> 49:42.020
No.

49:42.104 --> 49:44.481
And yet you blab on
about something personal.

49:45.565 --> 49:49.736
- Well, you keep on ignoring my forecasts.
- Or just using my own judgment.

49:49.820 --> 49:53.407
Well, you didn't report it to anyone.
And people suffered for it.

49:53.490 --> 49:55.617
Do you know about the cost placed
on the public's taxes

49:55.701 --> 49:57.494
to announce a severe weather warning?

49:57.577 --> 50:00.664
Billions of won spent
on a five percent chance of hail?

50:00.747 --> 50:02.374
I have to weigh the cost and probability.

50:02.958 --> 50:04.835
Still, you shouldn't ignore
a strong signal.

50:04.918 --> 50:07.963
When it rains in the morning,
and we told people the afternoon,

50:08.046 --> 50:09.715
the whole nation resents us for it.

50:09.798 --> 50:11.341
How would they react to a false alert?

50:12.300 --> 50:14.970
Ah, so you're really
just being conservative.

50:15.053 --> 50:16.304
What?

50:16.388 --> 50:19.057
You'll be blamed either way,
whether you get it right or you don't.

50:19.141 --> 50:21.184
So you prefer to save the money
and the budget.

50:21.768 --> 50:25.063
Dodge one bullet while you're taking fire
from two separate directions.

50:25.147 --> 50:26.648
Isn't that what you're trying to say?

50:30.736 --> 50:32.320
Don't worry about it.

50:32.404 --> 50:34.865
I know it's coming, the rain.

50:41.872 --> 50:43.248
Like your name.

50:43.957 --> 50:47.044
Yeah, Si-woo. Rain that comes on time.

50:47.878 --> 50:49.046
Lee Si-woo.

51:13.320 --> 51:14.654
It's going to rain.

51:45.769 --> 51:48.271
NAMSAN

51:48.355 --> 51:49.481
Whoa!

51:51.900 --> 51:52.859
Hey, sir.

51:52.943 --> 51:55.237
DONGJAK BRIDGE

51:58.031 --> 51:59.533
Yeah, I can see it.

52:01.409 --> 52:02.536
Wow.

52:08.083 --> 52:09.751
Jeez.

53:36.630 --> 53:37.923
For you.

53:38.590 --> 53:39.883
It's pouring.

54:14.793 --> 54:16.044
THIS IS URGENT

54:16.127 --> 54:17.629
GET BACK TO ME.

54:17.712 --> 54:19.214
Did you check with Ki-jun?

54:22.384 --> 54:23.468
WE SENT YOU AN E-MAIL CONFIRMING

54:23.551 --> 54:24.761
THE FINAL DRAFT
BEFORE WE START PRINTING

54:24.844 --> 54:27.138
We sent out an email
with the final proof of the design

54:27.222 --> 54:28.348
before we start printing.

54:28.431 --> 54:31.017
But the groom didn't get back to us.
Please check in with him.

54:31.101 --> 54:32.644
Honeymoon package
has been canceled…

54:32.727 --> 54:34.646
We have successfully canceled
your order of 200 mini gifts…

54:34.729 --> 54:36.523
We finished
the basting for your dress.

54:36.606 --> 54:38.191
We got a cancellation text.
Please get back to us.

54:38.275 --> 54:40.151
Your booking
has been canceled due to delayed payment.

54:40.235 --> 54:41.778
Please confirm.

54:48.201 --> 54:50.996
KI-JUN

54:52.664 --> 54:55.125
The person you are trying
to reach is unavailable.

54:55.208 --> 54:56.626
You will be connected to voicemail.

54:56.710 --> 54:58.962
Please leave a message after the tone.

55:19.691 --> 55:20.984
What'd she say?

55:25.613 --> 55:27.991
Ha-kyung hasn't responded.

55:30.243 --> 55:33.371
I think we lost the wedding hall
reservation now, Mom.

55:56.311 --> 55:58.313
Doors opening.

56:04.903 --> 56:06.279
Doors closing.

56:58.790 --> 57:00.417
The signals were simple.

57:00.500 --> 57:04.045
Hey, come closer.

57:04.129 --> 57:06.172
- Oh!
- Feel better now?

57:07.340 --> 57:09.884
Sometimes, they were sounds.

57:11.553 --> 57:13.721
Wow!

57:17.642 --> 57:20.353
Sometimes, they were colors.

57:47.922 --> 57:50.425
And sometimes, vibrations.

58:32.759 --> 58:35.428
They kept signaling to me…

58:37.222 --> 58:41.226
that nothing was safe in this world.

58:59.452 --> 59:01.621
Just in case.

59:10.547 --> 59:11.464
Oh, hello.

59:24.143 --> 59:25.478
So what is it?

59:26.104 --> 59:27.188
I got food for a trip.

59:28.815 --> 59:30.858
It'll stop raining early tomorrow morning.

59:31.442 --> 59:32.610
So no problem there.

59:38.908 --> 59:40.159
Oh, this?

59:40.243 --> 59:41.494
Just being thorough.

59:41.578 --> 59:42.912
We're not going camping.

59:42.996 --> 59:45.290
I got a nice cabin. Mm.

59:51.588 --> 59:52.630
We're over.

59:54.841 --> 59:55.800
What?

59:57.260 --> 59:58.553
We're over.

01:00:06.352 --> 01:00:07.604
Out of nowhere?

01:00:08.187 --> 01:00:09.397
Not nowhere.

01:00:10.857 --> 01:00:14.152
I've been wanting
to break up with you a long while.

01:00:46.434 --> 01:00:48.478
2 MONTHS LATER

01:00:48.561 --> 01:00:51.189
Wow, that star is so bright.

01:00:52.023 --> 01:00:54.067
The sky cleared up nicely.

01:00:54.942 --> 01:00:56.903
No, that's a satellite, sir.

01:00:56.986 --> 01:00:58.237
Hmm.

01:00:59.238 --> 01:01:01.532
Why do you have to be
such a stickler all the time?

01:01:01.616 --> 01:01:03.618
I know it's a satellite.

01:01:04.202 --> 01:01:05.328
Oh, okay.

01:01:07.455 --> 01:01:10.375
It's that trait
that makes me trust you always.

01:01:10.458 --> 01:01:12.627
Even more so than my own wife, I think.

01:01:15.922 --> 01:01:17.674
I wasn't a stickler when it mattered.

01:01:18.591 --> 01:01:19.717
What?

01:01:20.385 --> 01:01:21.803
You mean the day it hailed?

01:01:23.388 --> 01:01:25.014
Hmm.

01:01:29.227 --> 01:01:31.479
Director Choi, I think
you should check this out.

01:01:31.562 --> 01:01:33.564
Hmm?

01:01:36.859 --> 01:01:37.985
What?

01:01:39.153 --> 01:01:40.363
It's nothing.

01:01:48.830 --> 01:01:51.958
We were on standby all week
because of the fog.

01:01:52.875 --> 01:01:56.587
I know. You didn't report it
because you didn't want me to worry.

01:01:59.382 --> 01:02:00.800
I still should have gone to you.

01:02:00.883 --> 01:02:03.553
Do you think things
would have been different if you had?

01:02:04.303 --> 01:02:05.346
They wouldn't.

01:02:05.847 --> 01:02:07.640
I wouldn't have done anything.

01:02:08.141 --> 01:02:10.852
The fog in the West Coast area
was no joke.

01:02:11.644 --> 01:02:15.356
And we prevented
any major car or truck collisions

01:02:15.440 --> 01:02:16.941
along the highway, right?

01:02:18.276 --> 01:02:20.069
Nobody acknowledges things like that.

01:02:20.153 --> 01:02:23.114
Hmm. Why do you care
what they acknowledge?

01:02:23.197 --> 01:02:25.575
No one got hurt. That's what matters.

01:02:26.951 --> 01:02:28.453
Come back to us soon, sir.

01:02:28.536 --> 01:02:31.748
Oh? You didn't hear? I just resigned.

01:02:32.749 --> 01:02:34.876
How could you?

01:02:34.959 --> 01:02:38.629
I'm gonna live the rest of my life
doing everything I couldn't do before.

01:02:38.713 --> 01:02:39.839
Why? Why?

01:02:41.549 --> 01:02:43.217
My wife is so happy.

01:02:48.806 --> 01:02:49.807
So thank you.

01:02:50.767 --> 01:02:52.393
I couldn't have made the decision

01:02:52.477 --> 01:02:55.813
to retire early,
if the office didn't have you.

01:02:55.897 --> 01:02:59.859
I feel very safe
that you're ready to take the reins.

01:03:08.868 --> 01:03:12.246
I feel so close to drowning
all because I miss the signals.

01:03:18.544 --> 01:03:21.005
What you see in front of yourself
right now isn't everything.

01:03:21.088 --> 01:03:23.090
It's the same for life
as it is for weather.

01:03:23.174 --> 01:03:24.342
You have to wait and see.

01:03:24.425 --> 01:03:26.677
It's not always gonna be hailing for you.

01:03:27.637 --> 01:03:32.767
Sunny days, cloudy days,
rainy days, and snowy days…

01:03:34.811 --> 01:03:36.771
all come and go.

01:03:54.497 --> 01:03:57.208
PERSONNEL CHANGES
JIN HA-KYUNG: DIRECTOR

01:03:57.291 --> 01:03:58.918
What happens now?

01:03:59.001 --> 01:04:00.837
Well, she's smart.

01:04:01.462 --> 01:04:04.632
You think computers are doing
other people's jobs for them

01:04:04.715 --> 01:04:06.509
because they aren't smart enough?

01:04:06.592 --> 01:04:10.471
Experience is the most important quality
in a director.

01:04:10.555 --> 01:04:13.933
She's gonna be so high-strung every day,
lecturing everyone.

01:04:14.600 --> 01:04:17.311
But how? How's it gonna work, though?

01:04:18.145 --> 01:04:19.272
What?

01:04:19.355 --> 01:04:22.358
I mean, Mr. Han's going to return
from the honeymoon, right?

01:04:23.234 --> 01:04:25.444
Will they be okay when working together?

01:04:25.528 --> 01:04:27.321
What are they gonna do,
even if they're not?

01:04:27.405 --> 01:04:29.407
They can't quit their jobs
'cause they're fighting.

01:04:29.490 --> 01:04:32.785
The people around them
are going to be the ones that suffer, huh?

01:04:32.869 --> 01:04:34.620
We're all gonna be in some--

01:04:35.538 --> 01:04:37.415
- Hello, ma'am.
- Hello, ma'am.

01:04:37.498 --> 01:04:39.333
- Hello, Director.
- Hello, ma'am.

01:04:39.417 --> 01:04:41.043
Hello, ma'am.

01:04:41.127 --> 01:04:43.921
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

01:04:50.386 --> 01:04:51.512
You saw it, right?

01:04:52.138 --> 01:04:53.639
The promotion list?

01:04:53.723 --> 01:04:55.600
Yes, it was just posted.

01:04:58.185 --> 01:04:59.478
No.

01:05:00.229 --> 01:05:02.273
I'm talking about Mr. Han.

01:05:03.983 --> 01:05:05.359
You didn't see it.

01:05:06.652 --> 01:05:08.529
They canceled his transfer.

01:05:12.366 --> 01:05:14.368
He's good at dealing with the press.

01:05:14.452 --> 01:05:17.413
I guess the Administrator
thinks highly of him because of that.

01:05:17.496 --> 01:05:19.665
He wants to keep him by his side.

01:05:20.374 --> 01:05:22.793
Ah.

01:05:23.836 --> 01:05:25.171
You okay?

01:05:26.714 --> 01:05:29.425
I'd love for Chief Team Two
to still have you in charge.

01:05:30.885 --> 01:05:34.013
But you'll still see him around.
Is that okay with you?

01:05:41.270 --> 01:05:44.732
I mean, don't you wanna get on
the high-powered track?

01:05:45.441 --> 01:05:47.902
And work toward
a real leadership position, possibly.

01:05:50.404 --> 01:05:53.491
Well, you spent enough time
on a forecast desk.

01:05:54.408 --> 01:05:57.578
Are you saying that I should leave
the Forecast Bureau?

01:05:57.662 --> 01:06:00.873
There's an opportunity
for those commissioned to Grade 5

01:06:00.957 --> 01:06:02.458
to be sent to WMO.

01:06:04.710 --> 01:06:07.463
I mean, you have
more than enough experience.

01:06:07.546 --> 01:06:09.757
I can recommend you. Huh?

01:06:12.385 --> 01:06:14.345
You're talking
about Geneva, Switzerland, right?

01:06:14.428 --> 01:06:18.474
Yeah, Geneva. It's for a year,
but you can extend it too.

01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:23.604
The breakup wasn't the end
when it came to office romance.

01:07:12.653 --> 01:07:15.322
Tae-kyung, did you take
the TV from the living room?

01:07:15.406 --> 01:07:16.782
It's not there?

01:07:17.950 --> 01:07:21.037
Mom, did you take the TV
from Ha-kyung's place?

01:07:21.537 --> 01:07:23.330
Why would I take something from there?

01:07:24.040 --> 01:07:26.584
I wouldn't wanna risk
invoking Ha-kyung's wrath.

01:07:27.501 --> 01:07:30.296
Why? Is the TV gone?

01:07:30.379 --> 01:07:32.298
Uh, no. See you.

01:07:54.653 --> 01:07:56.155
Oh, my…

01:07:56.238 --> 01:07:59.658
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON
HAN KI-JUN

01:08:06.624 --> 01:08:08.000
No.

01:08:09.835 --> 01:08:12.213
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON
HAN KI-JUN

01:08:14.507 --> 01:08:16.550
Hello? So what's up?

01:08:17.510 --> 01:08:18.552
Huh?

01:08:19.178 --> 01:08:22.890
Ah, I guess I hit your number by accident.

01:08:23.933 --> 01:08:26.769
I'm doing good. Same as always, yeah.

01:08:27.603 --> 01:08:28.604
Um…

01:08:29.980 --> 01:08:32.483
Would you have taken the TV?

01:08:32.566 --> 01:08:35.236
Mm, yeah, I took it.

01:08:36.195 --> 01:08:38.447
- And the cooker?
- Yeah.

01:08:38.531 --> 01:08:39.907
The toothbrush sterilizer, too?

01:08:39.990 --> 01:08:42.785
You said to get everything together
and leave.

01:08:43.285 --> 01:08:46.872
I thought you meant
that I should take what I need. No?

01:08:47.748 --> 01:08:50.709
How… That's really what you thought?

01:08:51.335 --> 01:08:53.212
I meant get your stuff and leave.

01:08:55.381 --> 01:08:59.426
What's really mine and what's yours,
we split the cost of everything.

01:08:59.510 --> 01:09:00.553
I left the fridge, right?

01:09:00.636 --> 01:09:02.972
So doesn't that mean
it all roughly ends up equal?

01:09:06.725 --> 01:09:08.727
And when are we going
to deal with the apartment?

01:09:09.520 --> 01:09:13.524
So, Ha-kyung, I've been thinking.
How about, uh…

01:09:14.567 --> 01:09:17.361
I'll give half the money back to you,
and I'll take it all.

01:09:18.487 --> 01:09:19.572
All of what?

01:09:19.655 --> 01:09:21.657
We both put our names down on the title.

01:09:22.283 --> 01:09:24.368
And it'd be messy
to sell it together or whatever.

01:09:24.451 --> 01:09:26.996
This way, it's better for you too.

01:09:27.079 --> 01:09:30.082
You said I could keep it all
to make up for everything, didn't you?

01:09:30.166 --> 01:09:32.501
Yeah, I did say that.

01:09:32.585 --> 01:09:33.460
And then?

01:09:33.544 --> 01:09:35.963
The value went up. It went up a lot more.

01:09:36.589 --> 01:09:37.464
And so?

01:09:40.092 --> 01:09:42.344
Let's split it. Halvsies.

01:09:45.514 --> 01:09:47.099
As expected,

01:09:47.183 --> 01:09:52.479
a breakup wasn't enough
to get this bastard out of my life.

01:10:25.179 --> 01:10:26.555
Like the wind,

01:10:26.639 --> 01:10:29.850
an affair might not be visible at first,
but it will leave a mark.

01:10:29.934 --> 01:10:31.018
Now you're in. Go to work.

01:10:31.101 --> 01:10:33.854
I just got reassigned.
I'm on Severe Weather Forecast, Team Two.

01:10:33.938 --> 01:10:34.855
I've been transferred.

01:10:34.939 --> 01:10:37.650
I don't think Director Jin
will be here for very long.

01:10:37.733 --> 01:10:39.944
Han Ki-jun!

01:10:40.027 --> 01:10:41.737
- You leave me no choice.
- Do you want to fight?

01:10:41.820 --> 01:10:43.072
Director Jin.

01:10:43.155 --> 01:10:46.075
I wanted to check in
and see how you were doing.

01:10:46.158 --> 01:10:47.326
Cheers!

01:10:47.409 --> 01:10:49.536
I'll never date
a co-worker ever again.

01:10:49.620 --> 01:10:52.539
Really? Never is a strong word.
